## Teacher records API implementation

- Added `web/src/app/api/teacher/records/route.ts` for authenticated teacher GET/POST access.
- The route rechecks academy membership, current subject assignment, expected roster membership, and lead-teacher permission for attendance/common homework.
- The route validates draft/final input, test definitions and scores, absent/unexcused-absent restrictions, required values, optimistic versions, and the 10-day lock.
- The route writes multiple tables sequentially after validation. A database RPC transaction has not been added yet; atomic multi-table writes require a separate design decision.
- The current `/teacher/records` page remains a no-login, no-database demo and is not sent synthetic UUIDs. Connecting the page to the route requires an authenticated academy/session context.
- `npm run lint` and `npm run build` passed after the API changes.
